From ff9cb03d218862234a1d02c208fc19c496729348 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TechFusionReport <admin@techfusionreport.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 11:37:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebuild subcategory pages and site nav as static HTML, not
 client-rendered
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Same visual design ChatGPT shipped this afternoon (nav-group icon
dropdowns, pcb-panel hero texture, topic-card-grid, destination-card) —
recreated the right way: baked into HTML at generation time instead of
assembled in the browser from topic-data.js/topic-page.js/site-nav.js on
every page load. Matches what Agents.md already documents as repo
convention ("Build tooling: none — pure HTML/CSS/JS, no Node.js, no
bundler") instead of quietly contradicting it.

What changed:
- All 14 subcategory pages (ai.html, movies.html, etc.) rebuilt as real
  static files with real content in the HTML response — no more empty
  <div id="topic-root"> waiting on 3 scripts + a client-side posts.json
  fetch to render anything. Same content topic-data.js already had.
- Nav-group icon dropdowns baked into every page's header directly,
  instead of site-nav.js replacing <header> after the fact on every
  load (was shipping the OLD plain nav in the HTML response, then
  swapping to the new one client-side on every single page — a FOUC
  and a crawler/no-JS gap for zero benefit).
- topic-card-grid + pcb-panel on technology/entertainment/productivity
  hub pages baked in, instead of site-enhance.js rewriting the DOM
  after load.
- destination-card section on the homepage baked in the same way.
- Added About/Contact into the nav and a single consistent footer
  across every page — both had gone fully unlinked again from every
  core page (index/blog/technology/entertainment/productivity never
  linked to them at all, footers were each inconsistent).
- style.css?v= cache-bust unified to v=10 (was split v7/v8/v9 across
  pages, unrelated to this content, real pre-existing bug).
- Kept the one piece of site-enhance.js that's genuinely runtime
  behavior, not content: the latest-carousel scroll-accent-color
  interaction. Trimmed the rest out since it's now baked statically.
- Removed site-nav.js, topic-data.js, topic-page.js — fully superseded.
- dist/ regenerated via build.sh to match (untouched pre-existing
  drift in dist/ops/ and two graphics files left alone, not mine to
  decide).
- article-template..html.html and blog-post-template.html got the same
  nav/footer bake so every future- and legacy-shell post matches.

_build/gen.py is the generator (gitignored — no build step per Agents.md,
this is local tooling only, same as the first pass).
